    "product_faq_tPH4tG": {
      "type": "Product-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "left_U8xBjD": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m using a hormonal contraceptive",
            "dsc1": "<p>While you can certainly take Monthlies powder for its potential benefits, it's important to note that hormonal contraceptives, such as implants and pills, can affect hormone levels.  </p><p>Since hormonal contraceptives regulate your hormone balance, the efficacy of the powder might be compromised by the contraceptive method you are using.</p>"
          }
        },
        "left_78AnJL": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m on a fertility treatment",
            "dsc1": "<p>Fertility treatments often involve precise hormone manipulation.</p><p>It's vital to recognise that introducing new supplements, including the Monthlies powder, should be done under the guidance of your healthcare provider. The introduction of external supplements could potentially disrupt the intended hormonal adjustments of the treatment.</p>"
          }
        },
        "left_4BR8xr": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I’m already taking supplements",
            "dsc1": "<p>If you're currently using any medication or have been prescribed supplements for specific vitamin deficiencies, it's essential to consult your healthcare provider before incorporating Monthlies into your daily regimen.  </p><p>The Monthlies powder blend is designed to provide a fundamental level of hormone support, aiming to fulfil your body's requirements. This implies that you might not need to acquire extra vitamin and mineral supplements to address foundational hormone balance needs.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_Bt4xyP": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I have PCOS",
            "dsc": "<p>PCOS is a reproductive disorder characterised by the presence of cysts on the ovaries, elevated testosterone levels, and irregular periods. To be diagnosed with PCOS, a patient must exhibit at least 2 out of these 3 symptoms. However, several other symptoms are commonly associated with PCOS, including insulin resistance, difficulty losing weight, excess hair growth, hair loss, and depression.</p><p>If you're diagnosed with PCOS, then you're probably in more pain than our natural solutions can soothe all by themselves.</p><p>However, the blend of ingredients aims to support overall hormone balance, potentially benefiting those with endometriosis. <strong>It's advisable to consult our experts to determine the best approach for your unique needs.</strong></p>"
          }
        },
        "right_L8j6xV": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I have endometriosis",
            "dsc": "<p>Endometriosis is a medical condition that occurs when tissue resembling the uterine lining grows outside the womb, often in areas such as the ovaries or fallopian tubes. This condition can cause intense pain during a woman's menstrual cycle and, for some, even when they're not menstruating.</p><p>Diagnosis of endometriosis can be challenging, resulting in an average duration of 6-10 years before receiving an accurate diagnosis.</p><p>If you're diagnosed with endometriosis, then you're probably in more pain than our natural solutions can soothe all by themselves.</p><p>However, the blend of ingredients aims to support overall hormone balance, potentially benefiting those with endometriosis. <strong>It's advisable to consult our experts to determine the best  approach for your unique needs.</strong></p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "left_U8xBjD",
        "left_78AnJL",
        "left_4BR8xr",
        "right_Bt4xyP",
        "right_L8j6xV"
      ],
      "disabled": true,
      "custom_css": [],
      "settings": {
        "heading": "<p>Can I take <strong>monthlies </strong>if....?</p>"
      }
    },
    "product_bottom_faq_hhq647": {
      "type": "product-bottom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "left_6WrLgq": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I'm using a hormonal contraceptive",
            "dsc1": "<p>You can take monthlies while on birth control or hormonal contraceptive pills;<br/>however, it’s essential to understand that the effectiveness of monthlies may<br/>vary since your hormones are already being regulated. Additionally, monthlies<br/>could potentially interact with your hormonal birth control. To ensure safety,<br/>it’s always best to consult your doctor before adding any new supplements to<br/>your routine.<br/><br/><br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "left_pePbY6": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "Where can I find the full ingredients?",
            "dsc1": "<p><a href=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/Ingredients_EN.png?v=1739437663\" title=\"https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0708/7462/8371/files/Ingredients_EN.png?v=1739437663\">You can find the full ingredient list along with their dosages here</a></p>"
          }
        },
        "left_Whw3MP": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I have endometriosis",
            "dsc1": "<p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have endometriosis. While monthlies is not a treatment for endometriosis, it’s designed to support menstrual well-being by addressing some of the underlying triggers of period pain, such as hormonal imbalances, prostaglandin overproduction, and nutrient gaps. However, we always recommend you to check with your doctor before adding any new supplements to your routine, and check for possible interactions with medications.</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_jJrCAD": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I have PCOS",
            "dsc": "<p>Yes, you can take monthlies if you have PCOS, as there are many ingredients that may benefit those with PCOS. </p><p>However, monthlies is not meant to treat any medical condition so you should always check with your doctor before incorporating new supplements into your routine. Please also check for possible interactions with your medications (if any).</p>"
          }
        },
        "right_mKU3mh": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "Is monthlies suitable for a teenager?",
            "dsc": "<p>monthliesis recommended for females above the age of 16, as this is when their menstrualcycle and hormonal system usually begin to stabilise. For teenagers under the age of 16 (18 in Germany), we suggest consulting a doctor before introducing<br/>any new supplement. While monthlies is formulated with science-backed vitamins, minerals, and plant extracts that support menstrual health, it’s always best to get individual advice for the teen’s unique needs. <br/><br/><br/><br/></p>"
          }
        },
        "right_MTMG8w": {
          "type": "right",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading": "I am breastfeeding or pregnant",
            "dsc": "<p>It is not recommended to take monthlies if you are breastfeeding or pregnant, </p>"
          }
        },
        "left_hba7R6": {
          "type": "left",
          "settings": {
            "accordion_heading1": "I have IBS",
            "dsc1": "<p>monthlies can be taken by those with IBS, but since IBS can involve sensitivities to certain ingredients, we recommend reviewing our full ingredient list before introducing it to your routine. If you're unsure about how your body might react, especially to certain dosages and ingredients, it’s best to speak with your doctor or a healthcare professional who understands your condition.</p>"
          }
        }
      },
      "block_order": [
        "left_6WrLgq",
